-winning","book award","Darwin Award","preaward","awardable","awardee","awarder","awarding","awardment","misaward","reaward","unaward","unawarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d5d84513cbed275151","definition":"(in an examination) To give marks for a correct answer.","example":"Do not award marks for data from previous questions.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK, transitive","wordFamily":["Academy Award","award ceremony","award-winning","book award","Darwin Award","preaward","awardable","awardee","awarder","awarding","awardment","misaward","reaward","unaward","unawarded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/əˈwɔːd/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a8/En-us-award.ogg/En-us-award.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["Academy Award","award ceremony","award-winning","book award","Darwin Award","preaward","awardable","awardee","awarder","awarding","awardment","misaward","reaward","unaward","unawarded"]}